{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content pipeline/decisions/20260926-235952_route_change.md; Get-Content pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-T1-T2_diagnosis_20260926-235700.md; Get-Content pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-235700.md; Get-Content pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-235700.md'","aggregated_output":"# AdaRES_project 决策记录\r\n\r\n- **时间**: 2026-09-26 23:59:52\r\n- **类型**: route_change\r\n- **问题**: T1/T2 fixed native train64: admit either vacant server-2 slot?\r\n- **决策**: Reject T1 competitor-removal and T2 local-3D top-two; leave GPU0/1 unqueued\r\n- **依据**: T1 0.82133 vs B4 0.82256; T2 0.81370 vs B4 0.82256 and outside 0.82307; diagnosis/controls fail\r\n- **证据**: pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-T1-T2_diagnosis_20260926-235700.md; pipeline/research_work.json\r\n# Native diagnostic cycle: T1 and T2\r\n\r\n2026-09-26 23:57 Asia/Shanghai. Prepared monitor/goal preflight used once. Server-2 GPU0 key SSH, fixed first 64 ScanRefer training scenes, 1660 expressions, B4-E30 best checkpoint. Read-only inference, no validation tuning or training. Both probes repeated unchanged forwards with zero readout mismatches.\r\n\r\n## T1: Strongest-competitor causal influence\r\n\r\nB4's indicator computes an overlap-weighted peer context. T1 removed each query's highest-overlap competitor from that context and recomputed its trained head; the matched control removed its lowest-overlap peer. Among 388 material errors, the missed oracle gained more confidence from the closest-peer removal in 216, versus only 2 for the distant-peer control. The fixed closest-peer readout changed 47 selected queries and achieved 0.82133 mIoU, below unchanged B4 0.82256. Distant-peer removal changed none and retained 0.82256. The specific causal readout has no metric-aligned benefit. Inference peak reservation was 3.48 GiB, not training memory.\r\n\r\n## T2: Local 3D-feature support\r\n\r\nSeparately from S2's 2D features, T2 cyclically permuted 3D superpoint features inside each of the top two candidate masks, with an equal-count outside-mask control. Selected seed was retained in 1658/1660 inside and 1660/1660 outside interventions. Inside/outside mask IoU was 0.96619/0.99592; the intervention changes masks and thus cannot isolate confidence alone. Inside-mask confidence drop exceeded outside in 287/388 material errors. The frozen top-two matched-confidence rule yielded 0.81370 versus B4 0.82256 and outside control 0.82307. Full post-intervention mIoU was 0.80091 inside versus 0.82279 outside. Inference peak reservation was 6.02 GiB, not native backward or training peak.\r\n\r\n## Gates and disposition\r\n\r\nBoth fixed rules fail diagnosis/control improvement. Reject T1 and T2; no backward, training-resource qualification, isolated model/config, admission receipt, training sync, dispatch or queue mutation. Reopen only on new independently justified metric-aligned evidence with a prospectively specified matched native control, not a feature, weight, peer or top-k scan. This is bounded route exhaustion for this tick, not global scientific exhaustion.\r\n# Experiment Design - AdaRES_project\r\n\r\n2026-09-26 23:57 Asia/Shanghai\r\n\r\n## 1. Motivation\r\nGoal: \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\" Active 0/2, candidate budget 2. T1 tests trained competition context; T2 tests localized 3D support.\r\n\r\n## 2. Current Best Results\r\n| ID | State | mIoU | Acc@0.25 | Acc@0.5 | spmIoU |\r\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| B1 | complete | 0.5020 | 0.610 | 0.553 | 0.467 |\r\n| B4-E30 | champion | 0.5094 | 0.608 | 0.562 | 0.474 |\r\n| G1 | complete | 0.4980 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\r\n\r\n## 3. Analysis & Direction\r\nT1 closest-peer removal 0.82133 versus B4 0.82256; distant-peer control 0.82256. T2 3D top-two 0.81370 versus B4 0.82256 and outside control 0.82307. Fixed training-cohort diagnostics, not full-run metrics.\r\n\r\n## 4. Experiment Plan\r\nNeither candidate passed diagnosis/control gates. Reject T1/T2. No model/config successor justified. Future independent path requires a fixed matched native control, backward execution and training resource verification before admission.\r\n\r\n## 5. GPU Allocation Plan\r\nServer-2 GPU0/1 were 0% and 1 MiB each at the one targeted pre-probe query. GPU0 read-only probes finished. No post-probe occupancy claim or queue assignment. Server-6 excluded.\r\n\r\n## 6. Implementation Checklist\r\n- [x] Fixed train64 native read-only T1/T2 diagnosis and matched controls.\r\n- [x] Archived source probes and raw JSON.\r\n- [ ] Future candidate: native backward/resources, isolated model/config/tests, admission receipt, sync and safe dispatch only after all six gates.\r\n\r\n## 7. Risk Assessment\r\nT1 frozen-head recomputation worsens selection. T2 changes predicted masks along with scores; sensitivity is not a validated selector. Neither inference peak qualifies training resources. No novelty claim.\r\n\r\n## 8. Smell Check\r\nNo tuning-only, seed-repeat, pure ablation, banned or renamed-duplicate variant admitted. No peer/feature/weight/top-k scan proposed.\r\n\r\nStatus: NO ADMISSION. Bounded routes tested, no global exhaustion claim.\r\n# Motivation Review - AdaRES_project\r\n\r\n2026-09-26 23:57 Asia/Shanghai\r\n\r\n## 1. Goal\r\nAdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515. B1 0.5020; B4-E30 0.5094; target gap 0.0056. Constraints/bans checked: server-2 GPU0/1 only, one task per GPU, released backbone/project decoder, fixed B2/B4 continuation, required metric/resource reporting, no validation scans.\r\n\r\n## 2. Story Status\r\n| Hypothesis | Status | Evidence | Gap |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Query competition | Partial | B4-E30 0.5094 | Target unmet |\r\n| Competitor influence | Negative | T1 fixed readout 0.82133 vs B4 0.82256 on train64 | No selector benefit |\r\n| Local 3D support | Sensitivity only | T2 top-two 0.81370 vs B4 0.82256 and outside 0.82307 | No control-beating selector |\r\n\r\n## 3. Experiment Assessment\r\nB1 0.5020, B4-E30 0.5094, D1 0.5080, F4 0.5060, H5 0.5061, G1 0.4980. T1/T2 are native read-only probes, not trained experiments or validation evidence.\r\n\r\n## 4. Gap Analysis\r\nSelected-versus-oracle headroom remains, but neither competition counterfactual nor localized 3D reliance improves frozen selection. Active queries, full latency and training peak memory are unmeasured for these probes.\r\n\r\n## 5. Design Rationale\r\nT1 tests whether an overlapping competitor suppresses a missed oracle, with distant-peer removal as control. T2 tests local 3D support against equal-count outside-mask permutation. Failure narrows these exact mechanisms without legitimizing numerical scans.\r\n\r\n## 6. Next Batch\r\nNo admission. See `pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-235700.md`; resume only on an independent inference-available metric-aligned mechanism with all six gates.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
