alized 2D top-two retention rule: train64 0.82007 versus B4 0.82256 and outside-mask control 0.82271. Reopen only for a distinct predeclared inference-valid causal mechanism with matched outside control, paired native training diagnosis, backward and resource tests; no top-k/weight/feature scan.\",\r\n      \"evidence\": [\r\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_s2_local_appearance.py\", \"sha256\": \"329596181325c439fb7e70cf2750871324e45856ad3555d2ecc3c3bfc22cd69f\"},\r\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-S2_local_appearance_train64_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"e4cbc3a2e3c04892c9e8226cc649987028c323f0a99d4cf2627cbde5fba61034\"},\r\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-S1-S2_diagnosis_20260926-232500.md\", \"sha256\": \"1ca3fc2a3a845e78d7fa15df37e63f907bb13186d9847255f9e83730532ec6d7\"}\r\n      ]\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-R2\",\r\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not train or tune the frozen peer-confidence propagation rule: product selection 0.79612 versus B4 0.82254 on 1660 training expressions, with 30 strict repeat mismatches. Reconsider only on independent causal evidence and a stable matched native control, not a peer-fusion scan.\",\r\n      \"evidence\": [\r\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_r2_peer_confidence.py\", \"sha256\": \"40e71d9594d91c20788903b873902fe2a5a32e836476979551a7d4919f7a53d2\"},\r\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-R2_peer_confidence_train64_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"2ea85d1cb1cd2d8d1008cdc21bdb40e136c8d8384c47c0ebee9d22ae1480f87c\"},\r\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-R1-R2_diagnosis_20260926-220200.md\", \"sha256\": \"0c1e78bbc0f974b02911f5116657cf516670b5ec9827ed97ec7a651d596793ce\"}\r\n      ]\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-T1\",\r\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not train or scan competitor-removal policies. Frozen closest-peer deletion lowered train64 mIoU to 0.82133 versus B4 0.82256; distant-peer deletion was unchanged. Reopen only with independent prospectively controlled evidence for a distinct mechanism.\",\r\n      \"evidence\": [\r\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_t1_competitor_influence.py\", \"sha256\": \"8dc3910497a7470ad3886e6b5808da5c6df29c2165e0d8a46507bd940cf74a0e\"},\r\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-T1_competitor_train64_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"814fa1ee7f462aadff3bd4a905d97b3b0d9b250710e45197cff288db42abd189\"},\r\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-T1-T2_diagnosis_20260926-235700.md\", \"sha256\": \"f0e1de67bb97a83fc32ec517527caad06dd2398d69a0beb00db92caf7aae2bd3\"}\r\n      ]\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-T2\",\r\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not admit the local 3D top-two retention rule: train64 0.81370 versus B4 0.82256 and equal-count outside-mask control 0.82307. Reopen only for a distinct inference-valid causal mechanism with matched native control, backward and resource tests; no feature/top-k scan.\",\r\n      \"evidence\": [\r\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_t2_local_geometry.py\", \"sha256\": \"c69d588069296f979f78a7b796e2d20313df53e4738adeaae487a374d1cc9688\"},\r\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-T2_geometry_train64_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"c9464e5b9b7b874b8e06bfb0c2031967142624d7369fd2d9c1c9438a8074a02e\"},\r\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-T1-T2_diagnosis_20260926-235700.md\", \"sha256\": \"f0e1de67bb97a83fc32ec517527caad06dd2398d69a0beb00db92caf7aae2bd3\"}\r\n      ]\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"design_cycle\": {\r\n    \"at\": \"2026-09-26T23:57:00+08:00\",\r\n    \"candidate_budget\": 2,\r\n    \"admitted\": 0,\r\n    \"attempted_ids\": [\"AdaRES-T1\", \"AdaRES-T2\"],\r\n    \"stop_reason\": \"independent_routes_exhausted\",\r\n    \"stop_detail\": \"T1 closest-peer counterfactual 0.82133 and T2 local 3D top-two 0.81370 both under B4 0.82256 on